// std.os.macos: the calls of macOS, their constants and their types, as the
// C headers of the standard library's 14.45 declare them, with C's names,
// for the build's architecture. Calling them is `unsafe`, and those that
// fail with the system's error number give `os.Errno`. macOS has no call by
// number: a program calls the system's library, as these do. `tondo api
// std.os.macos.<name>` shows one of C's declarations, and `tondo api
// --search <words>` finds them.
//
// ```tondo
// import std.console
// import std.os.macos
//
// fn main() {
//     match unsafe { macos.kqueue() } {
//         ok(queue) => console.println("a queue of events: {queue >= 0}")
//         err(error) => console.println("kqueue: {error}")
//     }
// }
// ```
